1
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:16,933
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:38,621 --> 00:00:39,456
What was that?

3
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:42,791
Why are you flustered?

4
00:00:42,792 --> 00:00:45,669
Two years of living together,
and a kiss shocks you?

5
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:47,963
- It was out of nowhere.
- What is this, a drama?

6
00:00:47,964 --> 00:00:49,299
Should I have set the mood?

7
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:54,303
I got you, didn't I?
You're not my boyfriend.

8
00:00:54,304 --> 00:00:55,387
Now, fess up.

9
00:00:55,388 --> 00:00:57,056
Tell me who I <i>really</i> am

10
00:00:57,057 --> 00:00:58,307
and who <i>you</i> are.

11
00:00:58,308 --> 00:01:00,642
You're sure I'm not your boyfriend
after one kiss?

12
00:01:00,643 --> 00:01:04,064
If kissing a girl like me flusters you,
it's one of two things.

13
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:07,192
Either you're not my boyfriend,

14
00:01:08,276 --> 00:01:09,193
or you're gay.

15
00:01:09,194 --> 00:01:10,445
I'm not.

16
00:01:11,696 --> 00:01:13,655
- You want to make <i>that</i> clear?
- Enough.

17
00:01:13,656 --> 00:01:14,741
Don't do that again.

18
00:01:15,325 --> 00:01:16,784
Just as I'm unfamiliar to you,

19
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:19,537
I also find my girlfriend,
who's forgotten me, unfamiliar.

20
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:25,168
Eat that and take your meds.

21
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:30,547
I'm absolutely certain.

22
00:01:30,548 --> 00:01:33,009
How is this
what two years together looks like?

23
00:01:39,099 --> 00:01:40,558
Sheesh, that woman…

24
00:01:45,688 --> 00:01:46,523
Eel?

25
00:01:47,273 --> 00:01:48,858
Goodness me.

26
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:51,151
I could've just eaten at home.

27
00:01:51,152 --> 00:01:53,780
Why'd you bring a late-night snack
all the way here?

28
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:57,241
You'd be hungry by the time you got home.

29
00:01:57,242 --> 00:01:58,617
Oh boy.

30
00:01:58,618 --> 00:02:02,247
And today's the day we finally open this.

31
00:02:02,831 --> 00:02:06,417
I wanted to hurry
and have a drink with you.

32
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:11,714
Let's toast.

33
00:02:12,298 --> 00:02:13,550
- Cheers!
- Hold it.

34
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:16,177
Instead of clinking glasses,

35
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:19,180
I'd rather bump something else first.

36
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:29,149
- Man, what the hell?
- What?

37
00:02:32,735 --> 00:02:34,154
Holy smokes.

38
00:02:34,946 --> 00:02:37,906
I thought you went home a while ago.

39
00:02:37,907 --> 00:02:40,034
I did, but I came back.

40
00:02:43,204 --> 00:02:44,038
Do you

41
00:02:44,914 --> 00:02:47,792
just go for it like that?

42
00:02:49,252 --> 00:02:52,462
Without setting the mood or anything?

43
00:02:52,463 --> 00:02:56,134
Is it normal to just go for it like that?

44
00:02:57,427 --> 00:02:59,512
You're asking that at your age?

45
00:03:01,347 --> 00:03:02,598
I should get going.

46
00:03:02,599 --> 00:03:04,933
- No, please stay.
- No.

47
00:03:04,934 --> 00:03:07,519
- Tae-ha, I brought some eel.
- Right.

48
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:09,521
- No, I'm good.
- It's great for you.

49
00:03:09,522 --> 00:03:12,357
No, Tae-ha.
That ginseng liquor is good for you too.

50
00:03:12,358 --> 00:03:14,651
- Please…
- Drink up. I'll get going.

51
00:03:14,652 --> 00:03:15,486
But…

52
00:03:18,948 --> 00:03:20,533
Darn it.

53
00:03:26,206 --> 00:03:27,707
Looks like I

54
00:03:28,541 --> 00:03:29,458
interrupted.

55
00:03:29,459 --> 00:03:30,877
Oh, forget it.

56
00:03:33,796 --> 00:03:34,881
What the…

57
00:03:35,381 --> 00:03:39,551
Why the heck are your cheeks so red?

58
00:03:39,552 --> 00:03:41,137
Did you get beat up?

59
00:03:42,347 --> 00:03:44,556
Come on. You think I'd get beaten up?

60
00:03:44,557 --> 00:03:46,308
I'm asking because you're not.

61
00:03:46,309 --> 00:03:47,685
Tell me.

62
00:03:48,186 --> 00:03:49,812
Why are your cheeks on fire?

63
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:56,401
Seriously.

64
00:03:56,402 --> 00:04:00,197
You got spooked and almost blew it
over a kiss? And you call yourself a man?

65
00:04:00,198 --> 00:04:02,032
I wasn't spooked.

66
00:04:02,033 --> 00:04:03,743
Don't tell me it was your first.

67
00:04:04,827 --> 00:04:07,287
Don't ask. It's a pride matter.

68
00:04:07,288 --> 00:04:08,831
"Fried"? As in fried chicken?

69
00:04:09,415 --> 00:04:11,251
You mean it's "private."

70
00:04:11,876 --> 00:04:13,127
F-R…

71
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:15,338
You know?

72
00:04:15,964 --> 00:04:20,009
Yikes, I should've made sure
you hit some books too.

73
00:04:20,551 --> 00:04:24,721
Why would you try to use
our story as yours in the first place?

74
00:04:24,722 --> 00:04:28,600
Besides, it wasn't even a toad.
It was a snake.

75
00:04:28,601 --> 00:04:31,812
<i>At the very least,
you need to be able to catch a snake</i>

76
00:04:31,813 --> 00:04:34,856
<i>to make a girl swoon and fall for you.</i>

77
00:04:34,857 --> 00:04:37,234
If you told someone
they fell for you over a toad,

78
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:39,988
who'd believe that, you foolish toad?

79
00:04:40,571 --> 00:04:44,325
I don't know.
My mind totally blanked for a second.

80
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:45,952
Oh man.

81
00:04:48,037 --> 00:04:49,538
Unbelievable.

82
00:04:49,539 --> 00:04:52,833
I can't believe I'm seeing
the great Jang Tae-ha so humiliated.

83
00:04:52,834 --> 00:04:53,751
Goodness.

84
00:04:54,961 --> 00:04:58,005
Hey, since we're on the topic,
let me ask you something.

85
00:04:58,006 --> 00:05:00,966
What kind of debt
do you owe Prosecutor Go exactly?

86
00:05:00,967 --> 00:05:05,512
What could she have done to make you
save her from the brink of death?

87
00:05:05,513 --> 00:05:09,600
And why do you go as stiff as a plank
when you're with her?

88
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:13,396
You've actually met her before.

89
00:05:15,106 --> 00:05:17,108
I've met Ms. Prosecutor before?

90
00:05:21,821 --> 00:05:23,530
<i>Remember me when you make it.</i>

91
00:05:23,531 --> 00:05:26,534
Without me,
you would have missed out on a medal.

92
00:05:27,201 --> 00:05:29,912
When I win Olympic gold,
I'll shout you out in my interview.

93
00:05:30,955 --> 00:05:34,042
It was nice meeting you,
Mr. Future Gold Medalist.

94
00:05:40,006 --> 00:05:41,131
No way.

95
00:05:41,132 --> 00:05:43,593
That feisty high school girl

96
00:05:44,344 --> 00:05:45,345
is Prosecutor Go?

97
00:05:47,263 --> 00:05:48,598
We parted ways like that

98
00:05:49,974 --> 00:05:51,559
but met again eight years ago.

99
00:05:53,061 --> 00:05:55,396
8 YEARS AGO, JAPAN

100
00:06:34,435 --> 00:06:36,521
Why are you here?

101
00:06:42,235 --> 00:06:43,944
Who are you?

102
00:06:43,945 --> 00:06:46,196
Come on, this is a VIP room.

103
00:06:46,197 --> 00:06:47,657
Go on. Get out of here.

104
00:06:53,788 --> 00:06:54,705
Kill them!

105
00:06:58,042 --> 00:06:59,335
Charge!

106
00:07:14,350 --> 00:07:15,685
You bastards!

107
00:07:25,361 --> 00:07:26,779
Come here, you bastard!

108
00:07:40,293 --> 00:07:41,377
Hey.

109
00:08:05,109 --> 00:08:07,612
Please don't kill me.

110
00:08:08,446 --> 00:08:11,073
Count up what you've been skimming
and send over our share.

111
00:08:11,699 --> 00:08:13,451
Pull something like that again,

112
00:08:14,952 --> 00:08:16,537
and it won't end at this.

113
00:08:17,663 --> 00:08:19,207
Yes, understood.

114
00:08:40,144 --> 00:08:44,481
Sir, everything's been taken care of,
and it's drizzling.

115
00:08:44,482 --> 00:08:46,192
How about some sake?

116
00:08:46,692 --> 00:08:47,527
I'm good.

117
00:08:48,027 --> 00:08:50,862
Don't mind me.
Go relax and have fun with the boys.

118
00:08:50,863 --> 00:08:54,699
Come on. How could we relax
and have fun without you?

119
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:56,661
This card should do the trick.

120
00:08:58,704 --> 00:08:59,955
Thank you very much.

121
00:08:59,956 --> 00:09:00,915
Thank you.

122
00:09:01,415 --> 00:09:02,333
We'll see you later.

123
00:09:13,469 --> 00:09:15,096
That's him. Let's go.

124
00:10:15,406 --> 00:10:16,532
Get him!

125
00:10:18,909 --> 00:10:21,579
- Hey, stop right there!
- Stop!

126
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:29,128
Get him!

127
00:10:45,478 --> 00:10:46,937
Step aside. Move!

128
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:51,233
The hell do you think I am?

129
00:10:53,277 --> 00:10:54,362
Die!

130
00:10:55,738 --> 00:10:58,574
- What's this?
- What's this?

131
00:11:04,121 --> 00:11:05,081
Hop on, quick!

132
00:11:06,123 --> 00:11:06,957
Hurry!

133
00:11:16,634 --> 00:11:18,302
Get out of the way!

134
00:11:35,277 --> 00:11:36,445
Faster!

135
00:12:40,634 --> 00:12:43,637
- How did you--
- How did I know you were Korean?

136
00:12:44,138 --> 00:12:47,016
I saw you tell your friends
to have fun with your card earlier.

137
00:12:47,808 --> 00:12:52,188
But the people who followed you
looked pretty dangerous.

138
00:12:53,105 --> 00:12:55,733
There are a lot of yakuza here,
so you have to be careful.

139
00:13:04,950 --> 00:13:05,785
Something wrong?

140
00:13:11,123 --> 00:13:12,291
By any chance,

141
00:13:13,375 --> 00:13:14,668
have we met before?

142
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:26,055
2010 NATIONAL JUNIOR BOXING TEAM SELECTION

143
00:13:51,831 --> 00:13:52,790
I guess not.

144
00:14:05,261 --> 00:14:06,554
Yeah, I got away for now.

145
00:14:07,304 --> 00:14:09,389
I'll find my way back.
No need to come here.

146
00:14:09,390 --> 00:14:10,808
You guys move hotels. Now.

147
00:14:25,197 --> 00:14:26,698
What should I do?

148
00:14:26,699 --> 00:14:28,701
I don't have any gas to get back.

149
00:14:30,077 --> 00:14:33,372
I guess I rode a bit too hard earlier.

150
00:14:34,081 --> 00:14:36,040
Then we should call the rental company--

151
00:14:36,041 --> 00:14:39,211
It's the middle of the night,
so they'll be closed.

152
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:47,011
I guess we have no choice.
There's only one option.

153
00:14:47,511 --> 00:14:49,889
Time will pass, and the sun will rise.

154
00:14:50,389 --> 00:14:51,807
Let's wait until morning.

155
00:14:58,814 --> 00:14:59,773
You're bleeding.

156
00:15:00,858 --> 00:15:03,485
You must've gotten hurt earlier.

157
00:15:08,407 --> 00:15:09,575
That's got to hurt.

158
00:15:21,712 --> 00:15:24,256
All done. It won't get infected now.

159
00:15:25,341 --> 00:15:26,967
You carry Band-Aids with you?

160
00:15:27,635 --> 00:15:29,553
The backs of my heels chafe a lot.

161
00:15:30,971 --> 00:15:33,974
And you carry whiskey with you?

162
00:15:35,267 --> 00:15:38,061
I've only seen people carry these
in movies.

163
00:15:38,062 --> 00:15:39,605
Never in real life.

164
00:15:40,189 --> 00:15:41,773
You must really like alcohol.

165
00:15:41,774 --> 00:15:45,778
Or do you often feel like getting drunk?

166
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:53,993
Hey, wait a minute.
You're putting it away?

167
00:15:53,994 --> 00:15:55,829
It seemed like there was some left.

168
00:16:02,086 --> 00:16:05,838
What else is there to do on a long night?
We might as well drink.

169
00:16:05,839 --> 00:16:06,674
That's strong…

170
00:16:10,636 --> 00:16:11,553
Perfect.

171
00:16:14,890 --> 00:16:16,850
Did you come out here with your friends?

172
00:16:21,939 --> 00:16:23,064
I came alone.

173
00:16:23,065 --> 00:16:26,944
I'd been feeling down
since breaking up with my boyfriend.

174
00:16:28,654 --> 00:16:31,615
It's normal to struggle
to get over your first love, right?

175
00:17:13,866 --> 00:17:16,200
My name is Go Ji-won.

176
00:17:16,201 --> 00:17:19,079
But apparently my real name is Go Eun-sae.

177
00:17:22,374 --> 00:17:23,542
- Go Eun-sae.
- Yeah.

178
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:28,880
My mom left me at an orphanage
right after she had me.

179
00:17:28,881 --> 00:17:32,509
The head of the orphanage
registered me as Go Ji-won,

180
00:17:33,010 --> 00:17:36,138
but my name was Go Eun-sae
in my mom's maternity notebook.

181
00:17:36,638 --> 00:17:37,723
Pretty name, huh?

182
00:17:40,392 --> 00:17:41,727
That's why

183
00:17:42,519 --> 00:17:44,979
I'm pretty sure my mom loved me.

184
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:49,026
Who would give such a pretty name
to a baby they don't love?

185
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:50,486
Don't you think?

186
00:17:53,113 --> 00:17:54,698
What's your name?

187
00:17:58,869 --> 00:18:00,412
Jang Tae-ha.

188
00:18:02,247 --> 00:18:03,582
That's a really solid name.

189
00:18:05,876 --> 00:18:07,086
What do you do for work?

190
00:18:11,298 --> 00:18:14,175
You don't have to tell me
if you don't want to.

191
00:18:14,176 --> 00:18:16,011
As long as you're not a gangster.

192
00:18:21,266 --> 00:18:22,101
You see,

193
00:18:23,185 --> 00:18:26,229
I'm going to become a prosecutor
who catches bad guys.

194
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:27,689
I'm in law school right now.

195
00:18:33,278 --> 00:18:35,906
This place is so beautiful.

196
00:18:39,368 --> 00:18:42,621
I bet living somewhere like this
would feel like a dream.

197
00:18:48,919 --> 00:18:49,878
Take a picture of me.

198
00:19:07,104 --> 00:19:08,522
Thank you.

199
00:19:11,275 --> 00:19:12,734
I wonder how it'll turn out.

200
00:19:14,361 --> 00:19:16,154
You must like taking pictures.

201
00:19:16,155 --> 00:19:18,907
Yeah, I've been taking pictures
since I was a kid.

202
00:19:23,996 --> 00:19:25,998
Shall we take one together?

203
00:19:28,417 --> 00:19:29,418
It's actually…

204
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:34,631
my birthday today.

205
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:38,759
To celebrate.

206
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:39,970
Well?

207
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:52,524
What are you doing? Get over here.

208
00:20:28,852 --> 00:20:30,853
Back in elementary school,

209
00:20:30,854 --> 00:20:33,522
my eraser rolled over
to my desk mate's side,

210
00:20:33,523 --> 00:20:34,649
and all of a sudden,

211
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:36,984
they stabbed me in the butt
with their pencil.

212
00:20:36,985 --> 00:20:38,361
Isn't that ridiculous?

213
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:43,282
I'd always had two moles on my butt
just below where they stabbed me.

214
00:20:43,283 --> 00:20:47,912
The lead stabbed me in the perfect spot
to make a triangle with the two moles.

215
00:20:47,913 --> 00:20:50,707
So the mole on top is a different color.

216
00:20:53,168 --> 00:20:55,712
It's like a pyramid. So stupid.

217
00:23:17,062 --> 00:23:18,188
The sun's up.

218
00:23:34,287 --> 00:23:36,123
Happy birthday.

219
00:24:07,612 --> 00:24:08,530
All set.

220
00:24:12,159 --> 00:24:15,871
There's no need to thank me,
since I also had fun thanks to you.

221
00:24:23,587 --> 00:24:25,297
When we go back to Korea…

222
00:24:27,507 --> 00:24:28,967
can we keep in touch?

223
00:24:38,852 --> 00:24:40,020
If not, never mind.

224
00:24:48,361 --> 00:24:49,237
If we meet again…

225
00:24:51,907 --> 00:24:53,575
I'll make sure to pay back the debt.

226
00:25:00,582 --> 00:25:02,542
You better keep that promise.

227
00:25:04,044 --> 00:25:05,086
I'll be off, then.

228
00:25:46,878 --> 00:25:48,463
Damn.

229
00:25:49,130 --> 00:25:50,715
That's some fateful encounter.

230
00:25:51,967 --> 00:25:54,510
You know, all this time,

231
00:25:54,511 --> 00:25:57,889
I thought what we had here
was a film noir.

232
00:25:58,390 --> 00:25:59,599
But, man!

233
00:26:00,350 --> 00:26:02,893
Turns out it was a romance.

234
00:26:02,894 --> 00:26:04,436
It's not like that.

235
00:26:04,437 --> 00:26:08,525
I promised I would repay the debt,
and she said I'd better keep that promise.

236
00:26:09,901 --> 00:26:12,821
Besides, promises are meant to be kept.

237
00:26:13,780 --> 00:26:16,366
We call that the stuff of romance.

238
00:26:18,535 --> 00:26:19,744
Man.

239
00:26:20,245 --> 00:26:23,789
I thought you were a guy
who didn't know a thing about women.

240
00:26:23,790 --> 00:26:25,499
I'm proud of you, Jang Tae-ha.

241
00:26:25,500 --> 00:26:29,963
You have feelings for someone
buried deep in your heart.

242
00:26:31,673 --> 00:26:34,091
She didn't seem to dislike me before,

243
00:26:34,092 --> 00:26:37,429
so I don't get
why she's nitpicking everything

244
00:26:37,929 --> 00:26:39,306
and is suspicious of me now.

245
00:26:40,807 --> 00:26:43,934
Do you think it's because of my hairstyle?

246
00:26:43,935 --> 00:26:46,104
Maybe you weren't prepared enough.

247
00:26:47,022 --> 00:26:50,274
You should've bought some clothes
from a department store in Seoul.

248
00:26:50,275 --> 00:26:52,860
She's a young woman,
and you filled her closet

249
00:26:52,861 --> 00:26:55,195
with cheap clothes from the street market.

250
00:26:55,196 --> 00:26:57,991
Hey, your wife bought
all of those, remember?

251
00:26:59,326 --> 00:27:01,785
Jeong-hwa's taste is a bit old-school.

252
00:27:01,786 --> 00:27:05,789
And, to top it off, you're the one
who recommended that flowery blanket.

253
00:27:05,790 --> 00:27:08,126
Hey, don't women like flowers?

254
00:27:10,920 --> 00:27:13,423
That's what I thought too.

255
00:27:16,009 --> 00:27:18,762
Whatever. Look.

256
00:27:19,596 --> 00:27:20,847
There's only one way.

257
00:27:22,307 --> 00:27:24,768
You can't get flustered.

258
00:27:26,019 --> 00:27:28,187
Even if something like this happens again,

259
00:27:28,188 --> 00:27:31,024
you absolutely cannot get spooked.

260
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:33,859
When you've lived together for two years,

261
00:27:33,860 --> 00:27:37,906
you're bound to bump lips all the time.

262
00:27:38,865 --> 00:27:40,784
Some days, it gets pretty intense.

263
00:27:42,118 --> 00:27:43,078
And some days,

264
00:27:43,745 --> 00:27:45,580
it won't end at just lips.

265
00:27:49,668 --> 00:27:52,002
The heck? What are you, a traffic light?

266
00:27:52,003 --> 00:27:53,879
Why do you keep turning red?

267
00:27:53,880 --> 00:27:54,714
Me?

268
00:27:56,424 --> 00:27:58,093
Look at you.

269
00:28:05,183 --> 00:28:08,061
Judging by the kiss,
I'm certain he's not my boyfriend.

270
00:28:09,521 --> 00:28:11,064
Then why did he bring me here?

271
00:28:13,358 --> 00:28:15,443
Maybe he was my stalker who…

272
00:28:16,444 --> 00:28:18,780
He's way too unfriendly for that.

273
00:28:19,864 --> 00:28:21,866
Or was I kidnapped?

274
00:28:22,992 --> 00:28:23,993
Am I filthy rich?

275
00:28:26,287 --> 00:28:28,997
Seriously, what is all this?

276
00:28:28,998 --> 00:28:31,751
I'm absolutely clueless.

277
00:28:45,223 --> 00:28:46,224
Good job.

278
00:29:02,574 --> 00:29:03,742
I've got a headache.

279
00:30:16,940 --> 00:30:17,774
What is it?

280
00:30:19,859 --> 00:30:20,860
Let's have breakfast.

281
00:30:21,528 --> 00:30:22,820
I'm not hungry.

282
00:30:22,821 --> 00:30:25,323
You didn't even touch the sushi
I brought last night.

283
00:30:27,617 --> 00:30:30,410
How could I eat it
when I don't know what's in it?

284
00:30:30,411 --> 00:30:32,455
Since it's from my non-boyfriend.

285
00:30:35,834 --> 00:30:37,418
If you can't trust me,

286
00:30:38,294 --> 00:30:40,088
at least buy yourself something to eat.

287
00:30:40,630 --> 00:30:41,881
You shouldn't starve.

288
00:30:56,437 --> 00:31:00,190
Everything must feel unfamiliar,
so I wanted to stay with you,

289
00:31:00,191 --> 00:31:02,277
but I have somewhere to be today.

290
00:31:02,861 --> 00:31:04,028
It's something important.

291
00:31:04,571 --> 00:31:05,487
I'm sorry.

292
00:31:05,488 --> 00:31:07,365
It's <i>totally</i> fine.

293
00:31:07,866 --> 00:31:09,324
I couldn't care less.

294
00:31:09,325 --> 00:31:11,536
Still, being alone might be a bit weird,

295
00:31:12,287 --> 00:31:13,371
so I invited someone.

296
00:31:16,457 --> 00:31:19,459
It's been a while, Ms. Eun-sae.

297
00:31:19,460 --> 00:31:21,713
We've met before too?

298
00:31:23,339 --> 00:31:24,799
Well, of course.

299
00:31:25,383 --> 00:31:27,802
I was your closest friend in the village.

300
00:31:28,386 --> 00:31:29,387
Sorry?

301
00:31:30,138 --> 00:31:32,973
Well, then. Please take good care of her.

302
00:31:32,974 --> 00:31:35,017
Sure. Don't worry and go.

303
00:31:35,018 --> 00:31:35,852
Go on.

304
00:31:40,690 --> 00:31:41,566
I won't be late.

305
00:31:49,449 --> 00:31:51,742
I guess he doesn't wear sweats
all the time.

306
00:31:51,743 --> 00:31:53,828
Quite dashing, isn't he?

307
00:31:54,370 --> 00:31:57,373
Men look best in suits.

308
00:31:59,083 --> 00:32:03,212
My husband in a suit would knock
Park Bo-gum right out of the park.

309
00:32:03,713 --> 00:32:05,757
There's such a man in this village?

310
00:32:16,684 --> 00:32:17,560
You look different.

311
00:32:21,189 --> 00:32:23,024
So you cleared out your place in Seoul.

312
00:32:25,485 --> 00:32:26,319
Yes, sir.

313
00:32:26,861 --> 00:32:28,446
Thank you for everything.

314
00:32:29,781 --> 00:32:31,783
I know you like wine,
so I got this for you.

315
00:32:33,159 --> 00:32:34,035
Please accept it.

316
00:32:36,037 --> 00:32:38,872
A parting gift, is it?

317
00:32:38,873 --> 00:32:43,251
It's nothing compared to how
you've taken care of me over the years.

318
00:32:43,252 --> 00:32:46,881
A bottle of wine worth 100 million won
is nothing?

319
00:32:49,968 --> 00:32:51,177
Tell me, is this real?

320
00:32:52,303 --> 00:32:53,137
Sorry?

321
00:32:54,097 --> 00:32:57,266
Romanée-Conti is a wine
that has a lot of counterfeits.

322
00:32:58,601 --> 00:33:00,770
I paid full price
at a wine auction in Spain.

323
00:33:01,646 --> 00:33:02,730
It's authentic.

324
00:33:03,314 --> 00:33:06,818
Turns out, money isn't a reliable way
to tell what's real from what's fake.

325
00:33:07,527 --> 00:33:09,112
Sometimes, you pay the full price

326
00:33:09,862 --> 00:33:11,614
and still get fooled.

327
00:33:15,410 --> 00:33:17,912
I would never give you anything fake, sir.

328
00:33:18,496 --> 00:33:19,705
Of course not.

329
00:33:19,706 --> 00:33:20,957
Jang Tae-ha.

330
00:33:22,417 --> 00:33:24,377
You've never once disappointed me.

331
00:33:25,712 --> 00:33:27,088
I don't know about the others,

332
00:33:27,797 --> 00:33:28,840
but I trust you.

333
00:33:34,053 --> 00:33:35,179
So what's the plan?

334
00:33:36,305 --> 00:33:37,724
I'll put my gloves back on.

335
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:47,525
Boxing?

336
00:33:49,193 --> 00:33:50,193
Yes, sir.

337
00:33:50,194 --> 00:33:51,362
So…

338
00:33:56,409 --> 00:33:57,994
I'm returning this to you.

339
00:34:03,332 --> 00:34:05,376
It's a gift for taking off your gloves.

340
00:34:06,252 --> 00:34:09,505
From now on, get in fights
that reek of blood, not sweat.

341
00:34:19,766 --> 00:34:22,517
GUJIN TAFFY VILLAGE

342
00:34:22,518 --> 00:34:25,188
That place has great braised monkfish.

343
00:34:26,939 --> 00:34:31,110
And this place
does an amazing pollack stew.

344
00:34:31,694 --> 00:34:33,112
What would you like?

345
00:34:34,113 --> 00:34:37,532
You claim we were close,
but you don't know a thing about me.

346
00:34:37,533 --> 00:34:39,535
I don't like spicy foods.

347
00:34:40,119 --> 00:34:42,872
I didn't eat anything smothered in sauce
at the hospital.

348
00:34:44,290 --> 00:34:45,582
Is that so?

349
00:34:45,583 --> 00:34:49,045
So you can drop the act now.
I don't believe you.

350
00:34:50,213 --> 00:34:53,882
I'm going to figure out
why Mr. Jang Tae-ha is lying

351
00:34:53,883 --> 00:34:55,258
just to keep me here.

352
00:34:55,259 --> 00:34:56,468
Okay.

353
00:34:56,469 --> 00:34:57,969
Then why don't we eat

354
00:34:57,970 --> 00:35:02,517
the tofu poke you used to love
and figure it out?

355
00:35:03,976 --> 00:35:05,435
Have you tried tofu poke?

356
00:35:05,436 --> 00:35:07,437
It's delicious.

357
00:35:07,438 --> 00:35:09,648
You don't eat rice
because you're on a diet.

358
00:35:09,649 --> 00:35:12,902
If you want to slim down, it's all about
going hard on your meal plan.

359
00:35:13,986 --> 00:35:15,029
I know all about you.

360
00:35:16,697 --> 00:35:20,284
If you don't believe me,
figure things out on your own.

361
00:35:21,202 --> 00:35:22,786
Or don't.

362
00:35:22,787 --> 00:35:24,496
Boy, the weather's nice.

363
00:35:24,497 --> 00:35:26,790
Maybe I'll stop by the gym?

364
00:35:26,791 --> 00:35:29,543
Come here and have some tofu salad.

365
00:35:29,544 --> 00:35:31,294
It's called poke.

366
00:35:31,295 --> 00:35:33,380
I only know about it because of Eun-sae.

367
00:35:33,381 --> 00:35:37,717
It just looks like a bunch of raw veggies,
but that's what the kids call it.

368
00:35:37,718 --> 00:35:40,637
It's all just for show.

369
00:35:40,638 --> 00:35:41,472
Oh my.

370
00:35:42,640 --> 00:35:45,476
On your face, even a grain of rice

371
00:35:45,977 --> 00:35:47,937
looks like a diamond, honey.

372
00:35:51,816 --> 00:35:52,983
That's right.

373
00:35:52,984 --> 00:35:53,901
Park Bo-gum.

374
00:35:55,236 --> 00:35:57,155
What do you think? Isn't he handsome?

375
00:35:58,364 --> 00:36:02,952
When he's all dressed up, he really does
knock Park Bo-gum out of the park.

376
00:36:03,536 --> 00:36:06,080
If Park Bo-gum heard that,
he'd knock him out all right.

377
00:36:07,081 --> 00:36:09,750
So you're saying
I used to come here often?

378
00:36:10,459 --> 00:36:11,711
- Yeah.
- Of course.

379
00:36:12,295 --> 00:36:16,174
We used to eat together like this,
right here, all the time.

380
00:36:18,509 --> 00:36:19,594
You don't believe me?

381
00:36:20,094 --> 00:36:22,012
She's very suspicious.

382
00:36:22,013 --> 00:36:24,515
Let's see. What could we…

383
00:36:25,224 --> 00:36:26,308
Right.

384
00:36:26,309 --> 00:36:27,726
These coupons here.

385
00:36:27,727 --> 00:36:32,314
We collected so many
because you often ate with us.

386
00:36:32,315 --> 00:36:33,773
And what else?

387
00:36:33,774 --> 00:36:35,609
Darn, my eyes are so blurry.

388
00:36:35,610 --> 00:36:38,403
Then what's my go-to noodle order?
Three, two, one.

389
00:36:38,404 --> 00:36:39,989
- Spicy!
- Black bean… spicy.

390
00:36:42,909 --> 00:36:43,910
"Black bean spicy"?

391
00:36:47,288 --> 00:36:50,666
Do you honestly expect me
to believe any of this?

392
00:36:52,835 --> 00:36:55,588
Whatever. This neighborhood
has a psychiatrist, right?

393
00:36:56,505 --> 00:36:57,422
Why do you ask?

394
00:36:57,423 --> 00:37:00,175
I can't get a background check
with these fingers,

395
00:37:00,176 --> 00:37:02,094
so even the police can't help me.

396
00:37:02,678 --> 00:37:05,890
I figured I'd get my head checked
since I need my memory back fast.

397
00:37:12,396 --> 00:37:13,231
What is it?

398
00:37:13,940 --> 00:37:17,901
Is there any reason I can't get treatment
and get my memory back?

399
00:37:17,902 --> 00:37:20,279
Not at all.
You should get your memory back.

400
00:37:21,280 --> 00:37:22,572
- Yeah.
- What are you doing?

401
00:37:22,573 --> 00:37:24,032
Take her there in Bluey.

402
00:37:24,033 --> 00:37:25,909
Yes, of course.

403
00:37:25,910 --> 00:37:28,453
Let's go after we eat. Let's eat first.

404
00:37:28,454 --> 00:37:30,247
GANGJU CITY HALL

405
00:37:30,248 --> 00:37:31,707
Isn't it a bit odd?

406
00:37:32,291 --> 00:37:35,669
It's been over three weeks,
and not a single word from Prosecutor Go.

407
00:37:35,670 --> 00:37:37,004
Why are you so worried?

408
00:37:39,257 --> 00:37:42,510
You'd think you two dated for real.

409
00:37:43,010 --> 00:37:44,302
Have you grown attached?

410
00:37:44,303 --> 00:37:46,680
I went undercover
to derail the investigation.

411
00:37:46,681 --> 00:37:49,058
- I didn't expect this to happen.
- Exactly.

412
00:37:49,558 --> 00:37:52,561
If you'd kept her at the party,
we wouldn't be in this mess.

413
00:37:53,354 --> 00:37:54,688
Because of your mistake,

414
00:37:54,689 --> 00:37:57,107
I may have to concede a move
to Baek Sang-gil.

415
00:37:57,108 --> 00:37:59,235
Do you know how serious this is?

416
00:38:00,194 --> 00:38:03,029
Don't get all dramatic,
pretending you have morals.

417
00:38:03,030 --> 00:38:04,657
If you're a mole, act like one.

418
00:38:05,574 --> 00:38:07,576
Just do as you're told.

419
00:38:12,790 --> 00:38:16,210
Go Ji-won, just what were you thinking,
disappearing like that?

420
00:38:16,711 --> 00:38:19,838
Since they took your watch,
you probably couldn't do…

421
00:38:19,839 --> 00:38:21,507
Is this your trusty friend?

422
00:38:22,508 --> 00:38:23,342
Yeah.

423
00:38:26,429 --> 00:38:29,098
It better do a good job and not slack off.

424
00:38:30,474 --> 00:38:31,683
Don't worry.

425
00:38:31,684 --> 00:38:32,934
I have backup.

426
00:38:32,935 --> 00:38:34,144
That's right.

427
00:38:34,145 --> 00:38:36,188
The watch wasn't all.

428
00:38:38,399 --> 00:38:41,235
- This van is called Bluey?
- Yes.

429
00:38:42,111 --> 00:38:44,988
We named it because of its bluish color

430
00:38:44,989 --> 00:38:46,949
back when we were dating.

431
00:38:48,451 --> 00:38:51,287
Then it must be quite old.

432
00:38:51,996 --> 00:38:55,498
Vehicles may look different
on the outside,

433
00:38:55,499 --> 00:38:58,043
but the view from the inside
is always the same.

434
00:38:58,044 --> 00:39:00,378
What does it matter
if it looks fancy to others?

435
00:39:00,379 --> 00:39:03,257
What matters most is if it feels familiar
and comfortable to me.

436
00:39:12,975 --> 00:39:14,477
This…

437
00:39:17,730 --> 00:39:18,564
My goodness!

438
00:39:19,148 --> 00:39:21,274
This has never happened to our dear Bluey!

439
00:39:21,275 --> 00:39:24,194
Dear Bluey, are you okay?
Of course you're not!

440
00:39:24,195 --> 00:39:28,114
Familiar and comfortable is good and all,
but a vehicle has to be able to run.

441
00:39:28,115 --> 00:39:30,450
- What should we do?
- Just call the insurance.

442
00:39:30,451 --> 00:39:34,830
I'll call the insurance company,
and you head to the clinic, okay?

443
00:39:35,581 --> 00:39:39,376
By "that way," which way did she mean?
She could have given me proper directions.

444
00:39:39,377 --> 00:39:41,545
Is Bluey her baby or something?

445
00:39:46,050 --> 00:39:47,301
Oh no!

446
00:39:48,761 --> 00:39:50,011
Thank you.

447
00:39:50,012 --> 00:39:51,888
I thought I saw one over here.

448
00:39:51,889 --> 00:39:53,891
Where did it… Excuse me.

449
00:40:02,149 --> 00:40:02,983
Yes?

450
00:40:03,567 --> 00:40:06,236
Hello. If you don't mind,

451
00:40:06,237 --> 00:40:08,781
could you walk me
to that building over there?

452
00:40:10,032 --> 00:40:12,076
AN MENTAL HEALTH CLINIC

453
00:40:12,827 --> 00:40:13,743
Sorry?

454
00:40:13,744 --> 00:40:16,038
It's a waste to buy an umbrella
for a short walk.

455
00:40:18,165 --> 00:40:20,333
I'm also headed there, but I bought one.

456
00:40:20,334 --> 00:40:23,379
Oh, really? That's great.
If you're going that way, I'll join you.

457
00:40:24,672 --> 00:40:27,299
You don't need to worry about
tilting it my way.

458
00:40:30,845 --> 00:40:31,970
All right, then.

459
00:40:31,971 --> 00:40:33,806
- Excuse me.
- What the heck?

460
00:40:34,390 --> 00:40:36,516
- Why are you…
- Could you raise it a little?

461
00:40:36,517 --> 00:40:38,519
- Seriously, who even are you?
- I just…

462
00:40:44,108 --> 00:40:45,942
Would you like me to hold it?

463
00:40:45,943 --> 00:40:47,903
No, I'm good.

464
00:40:49,321 --> 00:40:50,322
I'm uncomfortable.

465
00:41:02,209 --> 00:41:03,377
Watch out!

466
00:41:14,138 --> 00:41:14,972
Your…

467
00:41:15,973 --> 00:41:16,807
Your hair…

468
00:41:25,149 --> 00:41:26,108
Take this…

469
00:41:30,237 --> 00:41:32,155
I'm sorry.

470
00:41:32,156 --> 00:41:34,741
I'm not very athletic.

471
00:41:34,742 --> 00:41:37,995
I was trying to turn us 180 degrees,
but I turned us the full 360.

472
00:41:43,667 --> 00:41:46,128
Not athletic, my ass.

473
00:41:46,837 --> 00:41:48,922
What a real piece of work.

474
00:41:48,923 --> 00:41:50,424
<i>Doors opening.</i>

475
00:41:52,176 --> 00:41:53,010
After you.

476
00:41:54,887 --> 00:41:56,388
I caught some of the splash too.

477
00:41:56,889 --> 00:41:58,474
Sure. Please wait a moment.

478
00:42:01,560 --> 00:42:03,394
- Hello, I…
- It's pouring outside.

479
00:42:03,395 --> 00:42:04,522
- Hello, Dr. An.
- Hi.

480
00:42:06,899 --> 00:42:07,733
Doctor?

481
00:42:11,028 --> 00:42:12,655
Shocker, right?

482
00:42:13,614 --> 00:42:14,490
Well,

483
00:42:15,699 --> 00:42:16,659
this is my clinic.

484
00:42:18,160 --> 00:42:19,827
We have towels, don't we?

485
00:42:19,828 --> 00:42:23,122
Yes, please, Hyang-seon.
The rain got her good.

486
00:42:23,123 --> 00:42:24,291
Oh my God.

487
00:42:30,256 --> 00:42:32,049
DIRECTOR AN GI-JUN

488
00:42:36,095 --> 00:42:37,303
So, you're saying,

489
00:42:37,304 --> 00:42:41,599
even though we can't treat you
because you're technically unidentified,

490
00:42:41,600 --> 00:42:43,601
I should help you get your memory back?

491
00:42:43,602 --> 00:42:46,146
Since I was a bit out of line earlier?

492
00:42:49,942 --> 00:42:52,443
- I'll pay for dry cleaning and umbrella.
- Seriously?

493
00:42:52,444 --> 00:42:55,905
You can continue your treatment
at the hospital you first woke up in.

494
00:42:55,906 --> 00:42:59,993
It's a small country hospital.
They can't give me professional treatment.

495
00:42:59,994 --> 00:43:03,371
I understand your situation,
but we have our own rules and procedures.

496
00:43:03,372 --> 00:43:07,333
Don't rules and procedures come second
to saving people with medicine?

497
00:43:07,334 --> 00:43:11,004
If it was an emergency,
of course I'd do that, but--

498
00:43:11,005 --> 00:43:12,422
This <i>is</i> an emergency!

499
00:43:12,423 --> 00:43:16,634
The man who claims to be my boyfriend
might not be my boyfriend!

500
00:43:16,635 --> 00:43:18,177
Then what would it be?

501
00:43:18,178 --> 00:43:20,430
It's a crime.

502
00:43:20,431 --> 00:43:21,974
Right now, Doctor,

503
00:43:22,474 --> 00:43:26,145
you could be standing by
and letting a crime happen.

504
00:43:26,770 --> 00:43:28,605
- What, me?
- Yes.

505
00:43:28,606 --> 00:43:29,607
But I'm…

506
00:43:30,190 --> 00:43:33,986
Couldn't he really be your boyfriend?

507
00:43:34,486 --> 00:43:37,031
I'm telling you, that's impossible.

508
00:43:37,531 --> 00:43:40,158
First of all, it makes no sense

509
00:43:40,159 --> 00:43:43,786
that I'm in this backwater taffy village
making taffy.

510
00:43:43,787 --> 00:43:46,122
Taffy village? I used to live there.

511
00:43:46,123 --> 00:43:47,040
What?

512
00:43:47,041 --> 00:43:49,418
I know every taffy shop.
Whose shop do you mean?

513
00:43:50,628 --> 00:43:52,171
It's Jang Tae-ha's grandmother's.

514
00:43:54,340 --> 00:43:55,174
Jang Tae-ha?

515
00:43:55,758 --> 00:43:59,261
The guy who claims to be your boyfriend
is Jang Tae-ha?

516
00:43:59,845 --> 00:44:00,679
Yes.

517
00:44:01,722 --> 00:44:02,556
Do you know him?

518
00:44:03,891 --> 00:44:06,477
Well… I see.

519
00:44:10,981 --> 00:44:12,524
DETECTIVE AGENCY

520
00:44:13,942 --> 00:44:14,859
Yes?

521
00:44:14,860 --> 00:44:16,944
<i>Firstly, no hospitals in the capital area</i>

522
00:44:16,945 --> 00:44:18,405
had a patient named Go Ji-won.

523
00:44:18,989 --> 00:44:20,448
Is that so?

524
00:44:20,449 --> 00:44:23,618
<i>But there was a hospital
that had an unidentified patient come in.</i>

525
00:44:23,619 --> 00:44:26,037
A female who looked to be
in her late twenties

526
00:44:26,038 --> 00:44:27,246
<i>to early thirties.</i>

527
00:44:27,247 --> 00:44:28,499
Where is that?

528
00:44:38,092 --> 00:44:41,052
According to our regulations,
we can't just treat you right now.

529
00:44:41,053 --> 00:44:42,720
Come back with Mr. Jang Tae-ha.

530
00:44:42,721 --> 00:44:46,849
We need at least one person who can vouch
for your identity, Ms. Go Eun-sae.

531
00:44:46,850 --> 00:44:49,228
Everyone in this place
is obsessed with Jang Tae-ha.

532
00:44:52,022 --> 00:44:52,856
- Hello.
- Hello.

533
00:44:53,732 --> 00:44:57,568
By any chance, the unidentified patient
who left yesterday morning…

534
00:44:57,569 --> 00:44:58,487
Is this her?

535
00:45:00,280 --> 00:45:01,572
I'm not sure.

536
00:45:01,573 --> 00:45:05,703
She has makeup on,
so I can't tell if it's the same person.

537
00:45:07,454 --> 00:45:08,956
It is the same person.

538
00:45:10,666 --> 00:45:14,253
- Sorry?
- It's the young lady who was in our room.

539
00:45:15,254 --> 00:45:16,170
Are you sure?

540
00:45:16,171 --> 00:45:17,839
Damn right I am.

541
00:45:17,840 --> 00:45:21,759
Her groom-to-be took her home yesterday.

542
00:45:21,760 --> 00:45:22,720
Her groom-to-be?

543
00:45:23,303 --> 00:45:26,724
Ma'am, do you remember
what he looked like?

544
00:45:27,307 --> 00:45:30,227
He was handsome like an actor.

545
00:45:31,186 --> 00:45:33,397
- Hong's…
- Hong's?

546
00:45:33,981 --> 00:45:36,524
Boxing Gym.

547
00:45:36,525 --> 00:45:38,402
That's what it said on the van.

548
00:45:38,986 --> 00:45:40,820
Hong's Boxing Gym?

549
00:45:40,821 --> 00:45:41,655
Yes.

550
00:45:47,870 --> 00:45:50,456
Those ladies are milling around
like gangsters again.

551
00:45:52,082 --> 00:45:55,042
They're no gangsters
but the S.E.S of Taffy Village.

552
00:45:55,043 --> 00:45:56,252
S.E.S?

553
00:45:56,253 --> 00:45:58,337
They might look tough,

554
00:45:58,338 --> 00:46:01,091
but they're actually lovely like fairies.

555
00:46:02,551 --> 00:46:04,887
Do they have different TVs
in Taffy Village?

556
00:46:13,979 --> 00:46:15,396
Ladies!

557
00:46:15,397 --> 00:46:16,273
- Hey!
- Goodness!

558
00:46:17,316 --> 00:46:18,566
I think she's parking.

559
00:46:18,567 --> 00:46:19,902
Who's that with her?

560
00:46:21,028 --> 00:46:22,612
It's that Gen Z kid.

561
00:46:22,613 --> 00:46:23,906
MZ…

562
00:46:29,620 --> 00:46:31,621
"Accurate spiritual readings"?

563
00:46:31,622 --> 00:46:32,456
Yes.

564
00:46:32,956 --> 00:46:35,751
Maeng-suk over there is a fortune teller.

565
00:46:36,919 --> 00:46:38,670
Is she now?

566
00:46:52,935 --> 00:46:53,769
Nothing.

567
00:46:54,353 --> 00:46:55,479
Sorry?

568
00:46:56,063 --> 00:46:58,231
Your face has…

569
00:46:58,232 --> 00:46:59,148
My face?

570
00:46:59,149 --> 00:47:00,317
…no writing.

571
00:47:01,318 --> 00:47:03,319
- There's no writing?
- Yeah.

572
00:47:03,320 --> 00:47:06,280
It means she can't have been
a judge or a prosecutor.

573
00:47:06,281 --> 00:47:08,533
Yeah, I can tell that much too.

574
00:47:08,534 --> 00:47:10,493
- Yeah.
- Then what was I?

575
00:47:10,494 --> 00:47:12,578
Then what could you have been?

576
00:47:12,579 --> 00:47:14,957
What could you have been? Let's see.

577
00:47:18,335 --> 00:47:22,005
Your name <i>is</i> Go Eun-sae.
Not much luck with parents or siblings.

578
00:47:22,589 --> 00:47:25,675
You were born in the fall,
in the Year of the Black Rooster,

579
00:47:25,676 --> 00:47:27,510
which means you have the Hwagae sign.

580
00:47:27,511 --> 00:47:32,139
That means you've got a knack
for the arts, pleasure, and even gambling.

581
00:47:32,140 --> 00:47:34,267
But if someone helps keep you in check,

582
00:47:34,268 --> 00:47:36,811
you can get through relatively unscathed.

583
00:47:36,812 --> 00:47:37,771
And that someone

584
00:47:38,313 --> 00:47:40,231
is Tae-ha, or so my spirit tells me.

585
00:47:40,232 --> 00:47:41,232
Yes.

586
00:47:41,233 --> 00:47:44,319
My, Maeng-suk. You're on a roll.

587
00:47:46,947 --> 00:47:48,448
I see.

588
00:47:50,993 --> 00:47:53,744
You know, while I was in the hospital…

589
00:47:53,745 --> 00:47:54,662
Yes?

590
00:47:54,663 --> 00:47:56,247
I did all kinds of experiments

591
00:47:56,248 --> 00:47:58,791
to try and find out what I was good at.

592
00:47:58,792 --> 00:48:03,797
- You did?
- But I was absolutely awful at drawing.

593
00:48:04,298 --> 00:48:07,091
And seeing how I couldn't figure out
the rules of Go-Stop

594
00:48:07,092 --> 00:48:08,843
even after watching the ladies play,

595
00:48:08,844 --> 00:48:11,137
I don't think I have a knack for gambling.

596
00:48:11,138 --> 00:48:12,973
So her reading's wrong?

597
00:48:14,182 --> 00:48:16,852
Be honest. You're not actually
spiritually gifted, are you?

598
00:48:18,061 --> 00:48:20,605
- What?
- You know everyone in the village.

599
00:48:20,606 --> 00:48:24,233
You probably know all about them,
down to the cutlery in their homes,

600
00:48:24,234 --> 00:48:25,610
so your readings were right.

601
00:48:25,611 --> 00:48:29,156
But you can't guess anything right
about an outsider like me.

602
00:48:30,407 --> 00:48:32,283
- It's pretty much a scam.
- What?

603
00:48:32,284 --> 00:48:34,453
- Scam…
- Scam?

604
00:48:36,455 --> 00:48:38,497
Enough. Get out.

605
00:48:38,498 --> 00:48:39,498
Out at once!

606
00:48:39,499 --> 00:48:42,669
My spirit is livid and refuses to tell you
anything else, so get out.

607
00:48:43,295 --> 00:48:46,964
What kind of spirit gets upset so easily
and refuses to say anything?

608
00:48:46,965 --> 00:48:50,092
Shouldn't spirits be more generous
than humans?

609
00:48:50,093 --> 00:48:52,136
What are you yapping about right now?

610
00:48:52,137 --> 00:48:53,180
You heard me.

611
00:48:57,100 --> 00:48:59,895
I can't give you this. Goodbye.

612
00:49:00,896 --> 00:49:02,648
I can't let you do that.

613
00:49:03,482 --> 00:49:04,942
<i>I</i> can't let <i>you</i> do that either.

614
00:49:07,819 --> 00:49:08,654
Why, you…

615
00:49:09,363 --> 00:49:11,657
What the hell do you think you're doing?

616
00:49:14,660 --> 00:49:16,452
What are you doing?

617
00:49:16,453 --> 00:49:17,495
I just…

618
00:49:17,496 --> 00:49:19,789
I won't let go until you pay me
for the reading.

619
00:49:19,790 --> 00:49:23,292
You didn't get anything right.
Why should I pay you?

620
00:49:23,293 --> 00:49:25,670
- Let go.
- You said you don't remember anything.

621
00:49:25,671 --> 00:49:28,005
So how would you know
if I'm right or wrong?

622
00:49:28,006 --> 00:49:29,173
- How?
- That hurts!

623
00:49:29,174 --> 00:49:31,342
- Hey, both of you. Let's talk it out.
- Let go!

624
00:49:31,343 --> 00:49:33,469
I can't let go until you pay me.

625
00:49:33,470 --> 00:49:35,180
Let go!

626
00:49:44,106 --> 00:49:45,481
- Who did that?
- I don't know.

627
00:49:45,482 --> 00:49:48,318
- Oh, revered spirit!
- Oh dear.

628
00:49:50,320 --> 00:49:52,280
The person who broke my revered spirit

629
00:49:52,781 --> 00:49:54,740
should pay for it, of course!

630
00:49:54,741 --> 00:49:56,742
Who else should pay for it?

631
00:49:56,743 --> 00:49:59,620
How do we know
whether I broke it or you did?

632
00:49:59,621 --> 00:50:01,248
- What did you say?
- What?

633
00:50:01,748 --> 00:50:04,417
The reason this happened
in the first place

634
00:50:04,418 --> 00:50:06,752
is because you refused to pay
for your reading.

635
00:50:06,753 --> 00:50:07,670
Exactly.

636
00:50:07,671 --> 00:50:10,297
If you hadn't tried to scam me
in the first place,

637
00:50:10,298 --> 00:50:11,674
I would have paid you.

638
00:50:11,675 --> 00:50:13,385
- Scam?
- Scam?

639
00:50:14,136 --> 00:50:15,511
- Easy.
- Ms. Eun-sae.

640
00:50:15,512 --> 00:50:16,679
- Ms. Eun-sae.
- Okay.

641
00:50:16,680 --> 00:50:20,267
Okay. Let's say that, in your opinion,
none of the readings were correct.

642
00:50:21,101 --> 00:50:24,145
Even so, Maeng-suk is your elder.

643
00:50:24,146 --> 00:50:27,899
It's not right for you
to talk to her like that. Don't you agree?

644
00:50:29,526 --> 00:50:30,652
- That's right.
- Ma'am.

645
00:50:31,486 --> 00:50:33,030
What's age got to do with it?

646
00:50:33,613 --> 00:50:36,783
If you're older, can't you be called out
for doing something wrong?

647
00:50:37,367 --> 00:50:39,243
Then I guess this grandma here

648
00:50:39,244 --> 00:50:42,581
is free to scam all of you ladies,
since she's the oldest.

649
00:50:43,081 --> 00:50:44,290
What do you mean?

650
00:50:44,291 --> 00:50:46,460
I'm only 17.

651
00:50:47,252 --> 00:50:51,423
Where did you learn
to twist people's words like that?

652
00:50:52,132 --> 00:50:52,966
I'm sorry.

653
00:50:54,217 --> 00:50:55,176
Tae-ha!

654
00:50:55,177 --> 00:50:57,053
Tae-ha, look at how she's acting.

655
00:50:57,054 --> 00:50:58,346
- Tae-ha.
- How could she…

656
00:51:00,015 --> 00:51:01,767
I'll pay for the damage.

657
00:51:02,768 --> 00:51:04,603
Tell me the amount with the reading fee.

658
00:51:06,855 --> 00:51:07,773
Why would you…

659
00:51:09,357 --> 00:51:10,900
Hey, wait. Let go of me.

660
00:51:10,901 --> 00:51:13,695
Come on, I'm not done talking.

661
00:51:14,529 --> 00:51:17,615
Seriously, let go of me!

662
00:51:17,616 --> 00:51:20,534
If you just come and apologize,
what does that make me?

663
00:51:20,535 --> 00:51:23,871
If you say you'll pay for the damage,
that means I did wrong!

664
00:51:23,872 --> 00:51:27,209
Should I have just let them bad-mouth you?
Better to settle it quickly.

665
00:51:27,709 --> 00:51:31,463
It's not about settling things.
It's about getting the facts straight.

666
00:51:35,133 --> 00:51:37,093
You trust me less than a shaman?

667
00:51:37,094 --> 00:51:38,428
Yes.

668
00:51:39,721 --> 00:51:43,183
- I wouldn't have gone if I didn't have to.
- Why is it so hard to believe me?

669
00:51:43,767 --> 00:51:45,601
Is it so hard to accept that we dated?

670
00:51:45,602 --> 00:51:46,895
- It is.
- Why?

671
00:51:49,231 --> 00:51:52,484
First things first.
You're not the type of guy I'd fall for.

672
00:51:55,862 --> 00:51:56,779
What is your type?

673
00:51:56,780 --> 00:51:57,697
Cha Eun-woo.

674
00:52:00,450 --> 00:52:01,367
Oh, come on.

675
00:52:01,368 --> 00:52:03,410
At the very least,

676
00:52:03,411 --> 00:52:05,330
you're not my type.

677
00:52:06,331 --> 00:52:09,126
And second, your kiss was too clumsy.

678
00:52:09,918 --> 00:52:12,503
You don't kiss like that
after two years together.

679
00:52:12,504 --> 00:52:13,505
And third,

680
00:52:15,090 --> 00:52:16,800
you're not warm.

681
00:52:18,802 --> 00:52:20,761
I went to the gym earlier.

682
00:52:20,762 --> 00:52:24,057
I could tell right away with the Hongs
that they're madly in love.

683
00:52:25,016 --> 00:52:27,977
The term "heart eyes" isn't just a saying.

684
00:52:27,978 --> 00:52:31,857
When you're truly in love,
you can't hide it. The eyes give it away.

685
00:52:32,357 --> 00:52:33,483
But

686
00:52:34,860 --> 00:52:37,612
your eyes are cold.

687
00:52:38,405 --> 00:52:40,406
I can't read your thoughts from your eyes,

688
00:52:40,407 --> 00:52:42,534
let alone your feelings for me.

689
00:52:45,495 --> 00:52:49,374
That's the ultimate reason
I don't believe you, Mr. Jang Tae-ha.

690
00:52:53,253 --> 00:52:55,630
Some people can't afford
to have their emotions read.

691
00:52:58,341 --> 00:53:00,092
Still going with the cool act?

692
00:53:00,093 --> 00:53:01,386
No one's like that.

693
00:53:22,616 --> 00:53:25,243
- I knew this would happen.
- What should we do?

694
00:53:26,786 --> 00:53:28,330
What else?

695
00:53:28,914 --> 00:53:30,623
Go and get me another pair.

696
00:53:30,624 --> 00:53:32,249
And leave you here alone?

697
00:53:32,250 --> 00:53:33,959
No, it's dangerous.

698
00:53:33,960 --> 00:53:36,253
What could be so dangerous
in a country village?

699
00:53:36,254 --> 00:53:38,089
At most, a deer might jump out.

700
00:53:38,965 --> 00:53:39,883
Should I…

701
00:53:43,345 --> 00:53:44,261
carry you?

702
00:53:44,262 --> 00:53:45,889
Don't get clever with me.

703
00:53:47,724 --> 00:53:49,851
You could have gone and come back by now.

704
00:53:58,985 --> 00:54:01,196
Fine. Wait here for a second.

705
00:55:29,326 --> 00:55:30,160
What happened?

706
00:55:32,203 --> 00:55:34,706
What's wrong? Are you okay?

707
00:55:37,459 --> 00:55:39,169
I'm not okay.

708
00:55:40,253 --> 00:55:43,006
I said I'm not okay.

709
00:55:44,966 --> 00:55:50,263
Put yourself in my shoes.
You have no idea how scared I am.

710
00:55:51,097 --> 00:55:54,933
I woke up and couldn't remember a thing.

711
00:55:54,934 --> 00:55:56,602
I'm told I don't have any family,

712
00:55:56,603 --> 00:55:59,272
I don't have any of my friends' numbers,

713
00:55:59,856 --> 00:56:01,523
and my so-called boyfriend

714
00:56:01,524 --> 00:56:05,153
doesn't seem like my boyfriend at all,
no matter how I look at him.

715
00:56:05,653 --> 00:56:08,114
But there's nothing I can do.

716
00:56:08,698 --> 00:56:11,868
I have no money and nowhere to go.

717
00:56:12,827 --> 00:56:14,871
And I don't even have my memory.

718
00:56:20,585 --> 00:56:21,753
See? I told you.

719
00:56:22,253 --> 00:56:26,006
I'm crying like this, but you're just
standing there doing nothing.

720
00:56:26,007 --> 00:56:29,593
What kind of boyfriend does that?

721
00:56:29,594 --> 00:56:33,723
How am I supposed to believe you
when you act like this?

722
00:56:36,393 --> 00:56:38,894
<i>Your eyes are cold.</i>

723
00:56:38,895 --> 00:56:41,105
I can't read your thoughts from your eyes,

724
00:56:41,106 --> 00:56:42,940
let alone your feelings for me.

725
00:56:42,941 --> 00:56:46,986
That's the ultimate reason
I don't believe you, Mr. Jang Tae-ha.

726
00:56:52,033 --> 00:56:53,159
I'll make you believe.

727
00:56:56,079 --> 00:56:56,913
What?

728
00:56:57,497 --> 00:56:58,832
So don't cry.

729
00:57:11,386 --> 00:57:12,887
First, put these on.

730
00:57:33,491 --> 00:57:34,492
Now listen carefully.

731
00:57:38,121 --> 00:57:39,998
I liked you from the moment I saw you.

732
00:57:43,960 --> 00:57:46,588
I wanted to ask for your name and number,

733
00:57:47,839 --> 00:57:49,214
but I couldn't say anything.

734
00:57:49,215 --> 00:57:51,259
I regretted that for a long time…

735
00:57:52,802 --> 00:57:55,096
and I couldn't stop thinking about you.

736
00:57:55,597 --> 00:57:56,848
I just hoped…

737
00:57:58,933 --> 00:58:00,393
to see you again someday.

738
00:58:01,978 --> 00:58:04,230
<i>And I was so happy when we finally met.</i>

739
00:58:06,316 --> 00:58:10,278
<i>Even then, I beat myself up for not having
the courage to tell you how I felt.</i>

740
00:58:12,155 --> 00:58:14,324
I vowed that if we ever met again,

741
00:58:14,949 --> 00:58:16,951
I'd never let you go.

742
00:58:17,994 --> 00:58:19,996
I made that vow over and over again.

743
00:58:22,290 --> 00:58:26,669
Seeing you hurt was unbearable.
It killed me.

744
00:58:27,295 --> 00:58:28,671
If only I could…

745
00:58:32,383 --> 00:58:34,219
I would have killed…

746
00:58:36,346 --> 00:58:38,598
every last soul who did this to you.

747
00:58:43,895 --> 00:58:45,939
I'm sorry I'm not Cha Eun-woo.

748
00:58:49,234 --> 00:58:50,944
And for not expressing myself well.

749
00:58:51,528 --> 00:58:53,947
You're the only woman I've ever liked,

750
00:58:55,365 --> 00:58:57,575
so I don't really know how.

751
00:59:01,079 --> 00:59:02,121
And as for…

752
00:59:04,374 --> 00:59:06,584
the clumsy kiss…

753
00:59:21,015 --> 00:59:23,016
That man is Mayor Ju's aide.

754
00:59:23,017 --> 00:59:26,396
He went undercover
to gather information on the prosecution.

755
00:59:31,651 --> 00:59:32,944
The clumsy kiss…

756
00:59:41,703 --> 00:59:42,537
Forget it.

757
00:59:45,123 --> 00:59:46,082
This one's for real.

758
01:00:13,985 --> 01:00:15,653
OUR STICKY LOVE

759
01:01:02,283 --> 01:01:06,245
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
